    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green. Done.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe spec: when more than 80 owners have already been created today, owner responses carry `bulkSignupWarning: true`, otherwise `false`. The existing test (`AcceptanceTest`) reads the flag back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so the flag lives on the owner response DTO, not just the create response.\n\nChanges, each kept to a single responsibility and reusing existing patterns:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`DailyRegistrations`** (new helper) \u2014 extracted the \"count owners registered on a given day\" primitive that was inlined in `EnsureDailyLimit`. This is now the single source of that count, following the same `findAll()`-iteration pattern as the neighbouring `Cities`/`Households` helpers.\n\n3. **`EnsureDailyLimit`** \u2014 refactored to call `DailyRegistrations.countOn(...)` instead of its own loop (no behaviour change; dropped the now-unused import).\n\n4. **`BulkSignup`** (new helper) \u2014 the warning policy: threshold constant `80` plus `warningRaised(repo)`, which counts registrations on the current business day (reusing `BusinessDays.rollForward`, matching how `ResolveRegistrationDate` assigns dates and how `EnsureDailyLimit` accumulates) and compares against the threshold.\n\n5. **Responders** (`RespondWithOwner` GET, `RespondWithOwnerCreated` POST, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated` PUT) \u2014 each now sets the flag on the mapped DTO via `BulkSignup.warningRaised(...)`. The policy is centralized in the helper; the responders just wire it.\n\n6. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 explicitly `@Mapping(target = \"bulkSignupWarning\", ignore = true)`, since the flag is a global request-time value not derivable from a single owner (documented that the responder sets it).\n\nI chose registration-date-on-the-current-business-day as the \"created today\" measure because that is the domain's canonical creation day (the same accumulation path the daily-limit rule and the test's `createMany` helper use), keeping the warning and the limit consistent.",
